 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your farm is miles away from the nearest sewer.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you build a little wooden outhouse over a shallow hole.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "In a few months, the hole is full.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And the smell brings flies from every corner of the farm.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you dig a much deeper pit, about two meters down.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now it lasts for years. But it still stinks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you run a black pipe from the pit up past the roof.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The sun heats the pipe, the air inside rises, and pulls the smell out through the top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "A handful of ash or sawdust after each use keeps the flies away.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But your drinking water comes from a well just a few steps away.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Rain soaks through the pit and carries germs down to the groundwater.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you move the outhouse at least thirty meters from the well, and downhill.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And you keep the bottom of the pit well above the water table.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "When it's almost full, you cover it with soil, plant a tree, and dig a new one.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Almost two billion people around the world still use one every day.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a toilet with no sewer at all. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
